# mini -> iumac — dedicated key for the mini's reverse reach into the MacBook
# (fixed verbs and the usage-tracker rsync pulls, via scripts/iumac-gate.sh). Kept OUT of
# config/ssh/authorized_keys and in this file instead, because it must be
# installed on the MacBook (iumac) ONLY, never on the mini itself: the mini
# holds the matching PRIVATE key on disk (~/.ssh/id_ed25519_iumac), so
# installing this public half into the mini's own ~/.ssh/authorized_keys too
# would let that private key authenticate back to the mini — turning an
# outbound-only credential into a standing inbound one on the machine most
# likely to be compromised first.
#
# `make authorized-keys` enforces the split by checking the present-human
# backend marker (`${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/secrets/backend`, "cache"
# = the mini) that scripts/remote-dev.sh and `make git-headless` already use
# to tell the two machines apart, rather than a second, independent hostname
# check that could drift from that one.
#
# FORCED COMMAND, NO PTY. `restrict` turns off pty allocation, port, agent and
# X11 forwarding and user-rc; nothing is re-enabled. `command=` pins every
# connection this key makes to scripts/iumac-gate.sh, a verb gate: it reads
# the requested command from $SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND, never evaluates it, and
# runs only the fixed operations the mini needs — a reachability probe, the
# human-queue dialog, notifications and URL opens, claude re-login, account
# snapshots, the iu-portal scrape and usage-tracker's rsync pulls — each with
# validated arguments. Anything else (shells, git, op, installers) is refused
# with exit 126. Least privilege: the mini's outbound credential carries
# exactly the operations it is used for. The gate also drops the 1Password
# agent socket before it runs anything.
#
# sshd runs the command through the user's shell, so $HOME expands there; the
# escaped quotes keep the path one word.
#
# `make authorized-keys` replaces any earlier line for this key by its key
# blob (so an older, broader line is pruned), keeps a timestamped backup and
# self-tests the gate afterwards; `make authorized-keys-rollback` restores the
# previous file. No `from=`: source restriction is the tailnet ACL's job (only
# tag:mac reaches tcp:22), and a Tailscale IP must not enter git.
restrict,command="/bin/bash \"$HOME/SourceRoot/dotfiles/scripts/iumac-gate.sh\"" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIABPkPsMROlF6nF0127jSEkNFlJ+Iqtkpy0T3nuMEOoJ mini->iumac
